+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Customers can create orders but cannot benefit from promotions: there is no way to attach a coupon to an order, so the payable amount is always the full amount. Letting a customer apply a coupon after ordering but before paying increases conversion and is the missing half of the existing coupon administration feature.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` accepting `{ "couponCode": string }`.
+- Validate the request, the order and the coupon in a fixed precedence order (see the change spec), returning the project's standard error shape with the documented HTTP status and code.
+- Compute the discount for `FIXED` and `PERCENT` coupons, apply the optional `maxDiscountCents` cap, and set `finalAmountCents = amountCents - discount`.
+- Persist the application atomically: update the order's `discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents`, `coupon_code`, insert a `coupon_redemptions` row, and increment `coupons.used_count` in one transaction.
+- Return HTTP 200 with the same body shape as `GET /orders/:id`.
+- Cover the feature with new tests. No schema changes and no new dependencies.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `order-coupons`: applying a single coupon to a pending order — request validation, eligibility and precedence rules, discount calculation, atomic persistence, and the resulting order representation.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+<!-- None: no existing specs in this project. -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/services/` — new application logic (rules, precedence, discount math).
+- `src/repositories/` — new persistence operations for orders, coupons and redemptions, including the transaction.
+- `src/routes/orders.ts` — new route parsing the id and body.
+- `src/app.ts` — unchanged wiring shape; the order service gains the coupon repository.
+- `src/db.ts` — unchanged (tables already exist).
+- Tests: new test file(s) alongside `tests/orders.test.ts`.
+- API: new endpoint; existing endpoints and their responses unchanged.
