+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Persistence layer and wiring
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `src/repositories/couponApplicationRepository.ts` exposing one method that writes the order's `discount_cents` / `final_amount_cents` / `coupon_code`, inserts the `coupon_redemptions` row, and increments `coupons.used_count` inside `BEGIN`/`COMMIT` with `ROLLBACK` on error. Verify with `npm run build` and a repository test that a valid apply updates all three tables in one call.
+- [x] 1.2 Wire `CouponRepository` and the new repository into `OrderService` through `createApp`, and register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` parsing the id via `parseId`. Verify with a smoke test that a valid apply returns HTTP 200 and a body shaped like `GET /orders/:id`.
+- [x] 1.3 Add an `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, body)` skeleton that validates `couponCode` (REQ-13) and throws HTTP 400 `INVALID_REQUEST` for missing, non-string, or blank values; verify with tests for all three cases.
+
+## 2. Eligibility and error precedence
+
+- [x] 2.1 Implement, in OrderService.applyCoupon and in the section-6 precedence order, the order checks: order exists (404 `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`), order is `PENDING` (409 `ORDER_NOT_PENDING`), and no coupon already applied (409 `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED`). Verify with tests including an already-applied order whose coupon code is also unknown, asserting `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED` wins.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement the coupon checks in precedence order: normalized lookup (404 `COUPON_NOT_FOUND`), status `ACTIVE` (400 `COUPON_INACTIVE`), `now < validFrom` (400 `COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID`), `now >= validUntil` (400 `COUPON_EXPIRED`), usage exhausted (400 `COUPON_USAGE_EXHAUSTED`), minimum not met (400 `MINIMUM_NOT_MET`). Verify with tests using an injected `Clock`, including a disabled-and-expired coupon asserting `COUPON_INACTIVE` and an exactly-at-minimum coupon asserting acceptance.
+
+## 3. Discount calculation and success semantics
+
+- [x] 3.1 Implement the discount math (FIXED, PERCENT floor, `maxDiscountCents` cap, `finalAmountCents`) and return the persisted order. Verify with tests for amount 10000 / PERCENT 20, amount 10000 / FIXED 1500, amount 100000 / PERCENT 20 capped at 5000, amount 999 / PERCENT 15 = 149, and mixed-case/whitespace `" save20 "` matching `SAVE20`.
+- [x] 3.2 Verify atomic success side effects (AC-09): after a successful apply the order carries the discount and normalized code, `GET /coupons/:code` reports `usedCount` incremented by one, `coupon_redemptions` gained exactly one row, the returned body equals `GET /orders/:id`, and the status is still `PENDING`.
+- [x] 3.3 Verify rejection is side-effect free (AC-08): applying a second coupon returns 409 `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED` and the order amounts, `usedCount`, and redemption row count are unchanged.
+
+## 4. Final verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run `npm run build` and `npm test` and confirm both pass, with the pre-existing tests in `tests/orders.test.ts` still green.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after review.
